# Backend Performance Rules

- Avoid blocking I/O inside request handlers; use async clients/drivers where possible.
- Batch or paginate expensive reads; never load unbounded datasets in one response.
- Add caching for hot, stable reads (in-memory or Redis) with explicit TTL and invalidation.
- Minimize repeated serialization work; reuse response models and avoid redundant transforms.
- Measure before and after optimization using latency/throughput/error-rate metrics.
- Move heavy background work (emails, exports, webhooks retries) off the request path.

## Example
```python
# Bad: CPU and I/O heavy work in request path
@router.get("/report")
async def report(): ...

# Good: enqueue job and return accepted
@router.post("/report-jobs", status_code=202)
async def generate_report(): ...
```
